    <!-- Module 3: Breast Care & Hygiene -->
    <string name="mod_care_title">Breast Care &amp; Hygiene</string>
    <string name="mod_care_subtitle">Evidence-based educational guide (Text Only)</string>
    <string name="care_card1_title">1. Monthly Self-Awareness Check</string>
    <string name="care_card1_body">Perform a gentle check 3 to 5 days after your period ends when breast tissue is least tender. Use the pads of your three middle fingers in small circular motions from the collarbone to the underarm and around the areola.</string>
    <string name="care_card2_title">2. Daily Skin &amp; Fabric Hygiene</string>
    <string name="care_card2_body">Cleanse the underbust fold daily with lukewarm water and mild pH-balanced cleanser. Pat completely dry before dressing and choose breathable organic cotton linings in warm climates.</string>
    <string name="care_card3_title">3. Bra Washing &amp; Rotation Care</string>
    <string name="care_card3_body">Wash everyday bras after 2 to 3 wears and sports bras after every workout. Rotate between at least 3 bras so elastic fibers recover for 24 hours between wears.</string>
    <string name="care_card4_title">4. Signs to Consult a Doctor</string>
    <string name="care_card4_body">Schedule a clinical checkup if you notice a new persistent lump, skin dimpling, nipple inversion, unusual discharge, or localized redness/warmth that does not resolve after your cycle.</string>

